# Information Design System

Swiss/Helvetica-inspired approach for high-density information displays. Based on principles from Müller-Brockmann and Vignelli. Use this when creating dashboards, detail views, data tables, or any interface requiring clear data hierarchy.

## Core Principles

1. **Grid-based structure** - Use CSS Grid with consistent column/gutter system
2. **Clear typographic hierarchy** - Distinct levels for labels, values, and supporting text
3. **Tight internal grouping** - Reduce gaps within blocks to create visual cohesion
4. **Section separation via padding** - Use section padding (not gaps) for vertical rhythm
5. **Vertical dividers for columns** - Create clear column separation in multi-column layouts
6. **Minimal decoration** - Let typography and whitespace do the work

## Grid System

```css
.info-container {
  /* 12-column grid base */
  --grid-columns: 12;
  --grid-gutter: var(--space-4);
  --grid-margin: var(--space-5);
  
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--grid-columns), 1fr);
  column-gap: var(--grid-gutter);
  /* No row gap - section padding handles vertical rhythm */
  padding: var(--grid-margin);
}

/* All direct children span full width by default */
.info-container > * {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
}
```

## Typography Scale

Use semantic naming that maps to design tokens:

```css
.info-container {
  /* Display - Large primary values */
  --type-display: var(--font-size-heading-xl);
  
  /* Title - Section headings */
  --type-title: var(--font-size-heading-md);
  
  /* Body - Primary content text */
  --type-body: var(--font-size-body-md);
  
  /* Caption - Secondary/supporting text */
  --type-caption: var(--font-size-body-sm);
  
  /* Label - Small uppercase labels */
  --type-label: var(--font-size-body-xs);
}
```

## Color System

High contrast for density and clarity:

```css
.info-container {
  /* Ink hierarchy */
  --ink-primary: var(--color-text-default);
  --ink-secondary: var(--color-text-secondary);
  --ink-tertiary: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  --ink-accent: var(--color-primary-default);
  
  /* Status colors */
  --status-positive: var(--color-success-default);
  --status-negative: var(--color-error-default);
  --status-warning: var(--color-warning-default);
  
  /* Structure */
  --divider: var(--color-ui-border);
}
```

## Section Pattern

Sections use padding for vertical rhythm, not parent gaps:

```css
.info-section {
  grid-column: 1 / -1;
  padding: var(--space-5) 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
}

/* Last section has no border */
.info-section:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
}
```

## Metric Card Pattern

For displaying key metrics with value, comparison, and insight:

```css
/* 3-column grid with vertical dividers */
.metrics-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: var(--grid-gutter);
}

.metric-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-1); /* Tight internal grouping */
  padding-right: var(--grid-gutter);
  border-right: 1px solid var(--divider);
}

.metric-card:last-child {
  border-right: none;
  padding-right: 0;
}

/* Label - uppercase, tertiary color */
.metric-card__label {
  font-size: var(--type-label);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  color: var(--ink-tertiary);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

/* Value - large, primary color */
.metric-card__value {
  font-size: var(--type-display);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  color: var(--ink-primary);
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
}

/* Comparison - colored by status */
.metric-card__comparison {
  font-size: var(--type-caption);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
}

/* Insight - supporting context */
.metric-card__insight {
  font-size: var(--type-caption);
  color: var(--ink-secondary);
  margin-top: var(--space-1);
}
```

## Two-Column Layout Pattern

For side-by-side information blocks:

```css
.two-column {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  gap: var(--grid-gutter);
}

.two-column__col {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-2); /* Tight internal grouping */
}

/* First column gets right border */
.two-column__col:first-child {
  padding-right: var(--grid-gutter);
  border-right: 1px solid var(--divider);
}
```

## Log/Timeline Pattern

For timestamped entries:

```css
.log-entries {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0; /* No gap - use padding */
}

.log-entry {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr; /* Fixed time column */
  gap: var(--space-3);
  padding: var(--space-3) 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
}

.log-entry:first-child {
  padding-top: 0;
}

.log-entry:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
  padding-bottom: 0;
}

.log-entry__time {
  font-size: var(--type-caption);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; /* Aligned numbers */
  color: var(--ink-tertiary);
}

.log-entry__content {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 2px; /* Very tight grouping */
}
```

## Status Badge Pattern

Solid colors for high visibility:

```css
.status-badge {
  display: inline-flex;
  padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2);
  font-size: var(--type-label);
  font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.status-badge--high {
  background: var(--status-negative);
  color: white;
}

.status-badge--normal {
  background: var(--status-positive);
  color: white;
}

.status-badge--warning {
  background: var(--status-warning);
  color: white;
}
```

## Alert/Insight Pattern

Subtle background with rounded corners (matches app design language):

```css
.insight-alert {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  padding: var(--space-3);
  border-radius: var(--radius-default);
  font-size: var(--type-caption);
}

.insight-alert--warning {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--status-warning) 10%, transparent);
  color: var(--status-warning);
}

.insight-alert--info {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-accent) 10%, transparent);
  color: var(--ink-accent);
}
```

## Key Spacing Rules

1. **Within blocks**: Use `var(--space-1)` or `2px` for very tight grouping
2. **Between related items**: Use `var(--space-2)` 
3. **Section padding**: Use `var(--space-5)` top/bottom
4. **Column gutters**: Use `var(--space-4)`
5. **Container margin**: Use `var(--space-5)`

## Responsive Behavior

Stack columns on narrow screens while maintaining grid integrity:

```css
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .metrics-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  
  .metric-card {
    padding-right: 0;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-right: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }
  
  .metric-card:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  
  .two-column {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  
  .two-column__col:first-child {
    padding-right: 0;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-right: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }
}
```

